The comment `@@@ If the element was not in the queue before removal, the method returns false.` specifies that when the element to be removed is not present in the queue at the start of the method, the return value should be `false`.

To express this in an assert statement:
- We can check whether the queue did not contain the element before the call using `\old(this.contains(o))`.
- If that condition is true (i.e., the element was not present), then the result of the method should be `false`.

Thus, the correct assertion is:

<code>assert !\old(this.contains(o)) => \result == false;</code>
